# Barkpark Caddy static-asset route — drop this INSIDE the site block that
# reverse-proxies the app, BEFORE the `reverse_proxy …:400x` line (and therefore
# before the maintenance `handle_errors` block in barkpark-maintenance.caddy).
#
# WHY. During a blue/green slot gap the app is briefly undialable and
# `handle_errors 502 503 504` answers EVERY request with the branded
# "Back in a moment" HTML — including `GET /assets/bp-paper-editor.css`. On
# 2026-07-07 that shipped an HTML 503 where a 13,194-byte text/css was expected:
# the already-cached JS mounted the PortableDoc canvas and it rendered
# completely unstyled. Papers looked destroyed; no data was touched.
# Serving the static tree off DISK ahead of the proxy means those requests never
# reach the app, so they never reach handle_errors.
#
# NO DIGESTS ON THIS BOX. api/ runs no `mix phx.digest`, ships no
# cache_manifest.json, and mounts Plug.Static without `cache_static_manifest`.
# Every file under api/priv/static has a STABLE name, so there is exactly one
# generation and old HTML and new HTML request the same URLs. Both slots already
# share this one directory (per-slot roots are _build_blue / _build_green; priv
# belongs to the checkout), so this changes WHO serves the bytes, not WHICH.
#
# `pass_thru` IS LOAD-BEARING. Not every /assets/* URL is a file — the reader
# references /assets/paper-surface/paper-surface.css, which the app answers. A
# plain file_server would 404 it; `pass_thru` lets a miss fall out of the handle
# and continue to the reverse_proxy, so app-served asset routes behave exactly
# as they did before (maintenance page included, during a gap).
#
# THE Cache-Control LINE IS NOT DECORATION. api/lib/barkpark_web/endpoint.ex
# serves these unversioned assets `no-cache` on purpose (`headers:` for the 200,
# `cache_control_for_etags:` for the 304) because a bare `public` let browsers
# heuristically serve a STALE Studio shell after a deploy. Caddy's file_server
# sends no Cache-Control at all; without this line that bug silently returns.
# Caddy's own ETag/If-None-Match handling still answers 304 (measured on 2.11.4:
# 200 + `Cache-Control: no-cache`, then 304 + `Cache-Control: no-cache`).
#
# The matcher mirrors `BarkparkWeb.static_paths()` — the exact set Plug.Static is
# mounted `only:`. The block carries NO slot-port token, so the blue/green
# ACTIVE_PORT grep and the port-flip sed pass over it untouched.
#
# SCOPE: the INSTANCE renderer only. deploy/site-deploy.sh's per-site
# `handle_path /sites/<slug>/*` + file_server blocks are a different concern and
# are NOT covered by this file.
#
# deploy/instance-deploy.sh injects this automatically (idempotent, validated,
# auto-reverting). For a hand-managed Caddyfile, paste it in and `caddy reload`.
# Replace <APP> with the checkout root (default /opt/barkpark).
#
# Example site block:
#
#   guerrilla.barkpark.cloud {
#       @barkpark_static path /assets/* /fonts/* /images/* /favicon.ico /robots.txt
#       handle @barkpark_static { … }
#       reverse_proxy localhost:4000
#       handle_errors 502 503 504 { … }
#   }
# BARKPARK_STATIC_ASSETS
@barkpark_static path /assets/* /fonts/* /images/* /favicon.ico /robots.txt
handle @barkpark_static {
	header Cache-Control "no-cache"
	root * <APP>/api/priv/static
	file_server {
		pass_thru
	}
}
